<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic</span></p>
<p>Automatically configures the best color profile pattern depending on 
 the appearance of the document to print.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic (Brighter)</span></p>
<p>Automatically configures the best color profile pattern to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic (Darker)</span></p>
<p>Automatically configures the best color profile pattern to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text</span></p>
<p>Optimizes the colors for text.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text (Brighter)</span></p>
<p>Optimizes the colors for text to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text (Darker)</span></p>
<p>Optimizes the colors for text to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic</span></p>
<p>Enhances mid-tone colors similar to those seen in photographs.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic (Brighter)</span></p>
<p>Enhances mid-tone colors, similar to those seen in photographs, to be 
 brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic (Darker)</span></p>
<p>Enhances mid-tone colors, similar to those seen in photographs, to be 
 darker.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation</span></p>
<p>Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics. This setting is best 
 for printing tables, graphs, and presentation materials that contain color.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation (Brighter)</span></p>
<p>Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation (Darker)</span></p>
<p>Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">CAD</span></p>
<p>Enhances reproduction of even colors that are true to the original.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">POP Display</span></p>
<p>Prints the color red more vividly. It is an optimal setting for the 
 POP display.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 1 (Bright/Yellow)</span></p>
<p>Enhances colors suitable for portraits.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 2 (Dark/Red)</span></p>
<p>Enhances colors suitable for portraits or food.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 3 (Darker/Blue)</span></p>
<p>Prints the color blue more vividly. Suitable for landscapes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 4 (Dark/Yellow)</span></p>
<p>Enhances dark-tone colors over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 5 (Brighter/Red)</span></p>
<p>Enhances bright-tone colors over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 6 (Brighter/Yellow)</span></p>
<p>Enhances brightness and contrast over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 7 (Darker/Red)</span></p>
<p>Enhances dark-tone colors and contrast over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading">Off</p>
<p>Prints colors without modification.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Use ICM</span></p>
<p>Corrects colors using the Windows ICM function.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Expand Gray Recognition</span></p>
<p>Checks every pixel and prints gray pixels (when the values of RGB are 
 equal or nearly equal) using black toner only.</p>
<p>This setting is available only if you have selected <span class="Term-Soft">K: 
 Expand Gray Recognition</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Gray Reproduction:</span> 
 list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free Color Management</span></p>
<p>Converts the colors used in documents to the barrier-free colors applicable 
 to Color Universal Design (CUD).</p>
<p>This setting is available only if you have selected <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free Color Management:</span> list.</p>
